      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Demons don't die easy. Our darkness follows us long after the night has passed. I want to live in the light, but it feels so far away. In the quiet of space, I hope we find peace and love. And I hope you and your friends can forgive me, some day. - Catra&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Best Friends Squad finds themselves on their next adventure after the Heart and the defeat of Horde Prime. They know that the universe needs to heal. But what can they do for each other? Many unspoken apologies linger between them. Catra finds herself square in the middle of them. Her actions as a Force Captain of the Horde may have been forgiven, but not in her mind. Not yet. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;___&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œYouâ€™re still Adora. Same jacket, same ponytail, same canvas pants. Youâ€™re the woman I remember. But then youâ€™re She-Ra. You can just be another person. You became a princess but youâ€¦â€ You didnâ€™t have to see, to do the things that I did.&lt;br /&gt;â€œHey, hey, hey.â€ Your fingers cup the sides of my head, thumbs on my cheeks. You gingerly rest your forehead against mine. â€œShe-Ra has nothing to do with what changed.â€ I feel you take a deep breath that wafts against my face. â€œBut a lot did. Can Iâ€¦ tell you about it?â€&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
